`--warn-unchecked-termination` is now on by default. `dafny verify` (and `dafny resolve`) warns about each trait with `{:termination false}` and each class or trait with `@AssumeCrossModuleTermination` in the code it verifies, since calls dispatched through them are not checked for termination and a program can prove `false` through them. Like the warning for an `assume` statement without `{:axiom}`, it fails the command unless `--allow-warnings` is given; `{:axiom}` on the declaration, or `--allow-axioms`, acknowledges the assumption and suppresses it. Programs that only use the standard library or another library are not affected. `--warn-unchecked-termination=false` turns the warning off, and the hidden `--legacy-no-unchecked-termination-warning` restores the earlier silence for migration (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/211).
